      "reason": "The reference on the nport is dropped before it is used. If this was the last reference, nport->release frees the nport object, and the following efc_sm_post_event(&nport->sm, ...) then reads freed memory (use-after-free)."
    },
    {
      "statement": "efc_sm_post_event(&nport->sm, EFC_EVT_SHUTDOWN, NULL);",
      "reason": "This accesses nport->sm after kref_put() may already have freed the nport."
    }
  ],
  "suggested_fix": "Post the shutdown event first and drop the reference afterwards: call efc_sm_post_event(&nport->sm, EFC_EVT_SHUTDOWN, NULL) and then kref_put(&nport->ref, nport->release). This keeps the nport alive while the state machine uses it. Another option is to take an extra reference around the event post."
}

